    <string name="privacy_policy_title">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_summary">How DeskControl processes data on this device</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">Last updated: July 25, 2026\n\nDeskControl does not transmit app usage or accessibility data to the developer or third parties. It has no analytics, advertising, crash-reporting, account, or developer-operated remote-server SDK. The Google Play edition communicates with Google Play only to display, process, restore, and acknowledge the optional Supporter Icon Pack purchase.\n\nData processed on this device\n\nDeskControl locally processes the list and identifiers of launchable apps, app launch history and pinned choices, external-display properties, Motion Mouse sensor readings, app preferences, and an in-memory diagnostic log. Accessibility access is used to identify and focus the active window on the external display and to send only the gestures, Back actions, and calibration key input initiated by you.\n\nActive app identifiers may appear in diagnostics. Logs leave the app only if you explicitly copy them to the clipboard and choose to share them.\n\nAccessibility Service\n\nDeskControl does not use accessibility access to make autonomous decisions, read passwords, bypass security controls, or transmit screen or accessibility data.\n\nPurchases\n\nThe Google Play edition offers an optional one-time Supporter Icon Pack processed by Google Play. The outside-Play edition contains no purchase functionality.\n\nStorage and deletion\n\nLocal data is excluded from cloud backup and device transfer. Clear DeskControl storage or uninstall the app to delete it.</string>
